OVERVIEW
========

     Galledis was created to ease putting Files online. It is a CNet
     Implementation of AmiExpress' Local Upload, but with many more
     Features.

     Imagine you just downloaded Tons of Files and want to put 'em
     online. Up to now you need a DirTool to copy/move the Files and
     you need to know where the appropiate directory is. With Galledis
     you log in, enter the UDBase and at the right prompt you start
     Galledis. A reqtools.library Requester will pop up asking you for
     the Files to be copied/moved. If you're ready, Galledis will do the
     Work for you and, new in v1.30, optionally auto-adopt the first File.

     But that's not all. Galledis is extremely configurable to your Needs
     (also for run-time through Command Line Arguments) and it supports
     multiple UDBase Partitions.


FEATURES
========

     + NEW: AUTO-adopting of first File possible
     + NEW: Can display Configuration used
     + NEW: Overriding of Port Restriction possible
     + NEW: German Documentation

     + The first and only Local Upload utility for CNet
     + Extremely configurable without external Configfile
     + Command Line Parser (? supported) allowing Run-time Configuration
     + Supports multiple UDBase Partitions
     + Ask Mode
     + Takes Advantage of reqtools.library's excellent Requesters
     + File Requester can open on CNet's Screen
     + No bad programming - highly optimized, unstolen Code
     + Easy to use


REQUIREMENTS
============

     Galledis requires:
     + reqtools.library by Nico François
     + rexxreqtools.library by Rafael D'Halleweyn
     + Move by Kai Iske
     + CNet 3.05c

     I tested Galledis with reqtools.library Version 38.1092,
     rexxreqtools.library 37.71, Move 1.10 and CNet 3.05c.

     Galledis will *not* work on CNet 2.63, e.g. due to changed GetUser
     Values! On request I might do you the favour and convert them.


INSTALLATION
============

     Just execute the supplied Script File "Install" or install by hand:
     - copy Move to C:
     - copy reqtools.library and rexxreqtools.library to Libs:
     - copy Galledis to PFiles:

     No matter whether you choose the lazy or the manual Way, you'll still
     have to add a new Entry to Section 4 of your BBSMenu File which starts
     Galledis. Don't forget to restrict Access.

     If you're a novice CNet Sysop: Start your favourite Text Editor
     and load the File 'CNet:bbsmenu'. Scroll down to the End of Section 4
     (UDBase) and add the following Line:

     <TAB>LUP |#0PFiles:Galledis} |`31
               ^
               `-- This is a CTRL-Q Character, ASCII Code 17!

     Notice the `31 at the End. ` initates a List of Access Groups which
     are allowed exclusively to run the Tool. So if you have a CoSysop with
     Access Level 30 you would write `30,31.

     Of course you can change LUP to what you want as long as it's not
     already used in the File.

     Also don't forget to change the Path if you installed Galledis
     somewhere else. If you used the Install Script PFiles: is the right
     Location.


CONFIGURATION
=============

     + Show Run-Time Configuration? (Variable: showconfig)
       If 1, everytime you're running Galledis you're informed which
       Settings apply NOW you're running it. If 0, you're not :).
       Default is 1. Command Line Form: Cx.

     + Operation Mode (Variable: opmode)
       If you want Galledis to copy _all_ Files, set this to 0. If you
       want Galledis to move _all_ Files, set this to 1. Setting 2
       enables Ask Mode which asks you for every File whether to copy,
       move or to abort.
       Default is 2. Command Line Form: Mx.

     + Default Path for the Requester (Variable: reqpath)
       This is the Path the ReqTools Filerequester will scan first.
       Usually this will be your Up- and Downloads Directory.
       If you use this from the Command Line do *NOT* use any Spaces !!!
       Default is 'DH0:'. Command Line Form: Rx.

     + Flush Requester Buffers? (Variable: reqflush)
       ReqTools features an internal Directory Cache. If you used Galledis
       once and start it again the Requester will remember the previous
       Contents. If you want to disable this Cache, set this to 1 (Yes),
       else specify 0 (No).
       Default is 0. Command Line Form: Fx.

     + Open Requester on CNet's Screen? (Variable: reqscreen)
       If you want the Requester to be opened on the Screen you started
       Galledis from set this to 1 (Yes), else specify 0 (No).
       Default is 1. Command Line Form: Sx.

     + Partition Select? (Variable: partselect)
       If you have one UDBase0: Assign, set this to 0. Or to 1, if you
       want Galledis to display you where the Files will be copied or
       moved to. If you have several UDBase Partitions, set this to 2
       to enable Partition Select.
       Default is 1. Command Line Form: Px.

     + Default Partition (Variable: defpart)
       Only required if you set partselect to 2.
       Default is 0.

     + Override Password (Variable: override)
       Password to override Port Restriction. See below for more Info.
       Don't use ALT or CTRL Characters!
       Default is "".

     + Log Override Attempts? (Variable: logoverride)
       Should Galledis log Override Attempts? 0=No, 1=Yes, 2=Full.
       See below for more Info.
       Default is 2.

     + Auto-adopt Files? (Variable: autoadopt)
       Should Galledis auto-adopt the first File? 0=No or 1=Yes.
       See below for more Info.
       Default is 1.

     + Adopt Orphans Command (Variable: aocommand)
       Some Sysops may have localized their system heavily...
       put the Command you use in the BBSMenu File here.

     As you have seen some Options have a Command Line Form. You can append
     one or several of these Options seperated by Space behind the Command
     you used to call Galledis. The Order doesn't matter.

     You needn't check this Docfile all the Time just to see what the
     Command Line Form of an Option is. Run Galledis with "?" and you'll
     get Online Help, just like with Shell Commands.

     If you disabled Display of Configuration and you just want to see it
     once, the Argument "C" will show it.

     Note that the last two Arguments will cause Galledis to exit immediately
     after finishing their jobs.

     Another Argument for the Command Line is "O" which forces Galledis
     to override Port Restriction. Normally Galledis can be run from a
     local Port only. If you for any Reason want to disable this Check
     specify Option "O" and enter the Password you specified in the
     variable override. If you set logoverride to 2, all Attempts to
     override are logged, if 1 only failed ones. Leave override empty
     to disable overriding at all.

     Last not least about the Auto-adopting. v1.30 goes a Step further
     than in previous Versions. You needn't know the first Filename
     anylonger. I already hear you saying "Amazing Feature"... it is
     simply not possible to auto-adopt ALL Files !!! I don't want to
     explain it here, if you're an advanced coder, you'll know why.


USAGE
=====

     Some Examples for valid Command Strings:

     LUP ?
     LUP M2 RHD1: P0
     LUP S1 RDF0: C
     LUP F1

     Invalid Command Strings:

     LUPM0          will cause CNet not to recognize the LUP Command
     LUP RHD1:P1    will make the Requester ask for "HD1:P1"
     LUP F1S1       will make Galledis ignore the Argument as it's not
                    supported
     LUP F3         will make Galledis print an Error Message because
                    the F Argument accepts 0 or 1 as Parameter only

     The overall Usage of Galledis is pretty easy and does not need to
     be explained, does it?

     Please refer to the reqtools.library's Manuals for how to use
     the Requester (if you need to). Multi-Selection of Files is done
     by clicking on the first File, then, while holding the SHIFT Key,
     clicking on the other Files.

     For Usage of the Move Commando type 'Move ?' or check its Docfile.


HISTORY
=======

     v1.21          16 September 1994 - Public Release
                    Move Routine now also works when moving from different
                    Devices. Also added Partition Select.

     v1.22          21 September 1994 - Internal Release
                    Added "Override Port Restriction" Feature.

     v1.23          24 September 1994 - Internal Release
                    Added Display of current Configuration.

     v1.24          26 September 1994 - Internal Release
                    Added more Checks to enforce Usage from Subboards
                    only - if you chose the wrong BBSMenu Area.

     v1.30          3 October 1994 - Public Release
                    Added Posibility to auto-adopt the first File
                    Added German Documentation.
                    Hmm, I'd rather say: translated in a hurry ;)


UPDATES
=======

     New Versions of Galledis and other CNet Tools by Logic will be available
     through various medias. You should take a Look at AmiNet's comm/bbs/cnet
     Directory as well as your local BBSes. Galledis is also FTPable from
     bkroom.apana.org.au, in the directory /pub/amiga/comm/cnet/. Furthermore
     Galledis is FIDO FREQable from Frontiers BBS, Buffalo, NY (1:260/121).
     Members of the UUCP Mailing List will get new Updates automatically as
     long as the File Size stays reasonable. Last not least you can download
     it directly from any of the Boards listed below.


